  "summary": "Malicious versions (1.26.1, 1.26.2) of the 'agent-framework' PyPI package act as a credential stealer. The malware uses a .pth file to execute on Python interpreter startup, harvesting environment variables, configuration files, and cloud credentials from Azure and GitHub. Collected data is Base64 encoded, zlib compressed, and exfiltrated via a POST request to a hardcoded webhook.site URL.",
